attempts.raw:
@start **The window opens on a single spine column.** Column 0, `rpsT`, is carried by 100% of chromosomes, persistent, in a region of plasticity in 0% of calls {S1}. The model names 99% of them, at 0.03 bits {S1}.

@variable **A fork follows at column 1**, `fimbrial family protein`, carried by 52%, the most plastic stretch of the window {S2, P}. The long spine, columns 6 to 37, `dnaJ` to `lplA`, is [[molecular chaperone DnaJ]] {S5, Q}. Through columns 68 to 71 a branch of 4 shell families runs in 26 to 27%, [[homoprotocatechuate degradation]] {S8.b68, Q}.

@model **The model names more genes on the spine columns than on the fork and variable ones**, 96 against 86%, and hesitates less there, 0.18 against 0.52 bits {M}. It hesitates most at column 1, a fork column, 1.97 bits {H}.

@end **The window ends in fork and variable columns.** Columns 50 to 79 are carried by 17 to 83% of chromosomes, in a region of plasticity in 6 to 57% of calls {S8}. The last column is `yjiJ`, in 17% of chromosomes {E}.

@whole **Across the window it names 92% of genes**, 0.32 bits on average, perplexity 1.4 families {G}. Inside a region of plasticity it hesitates more than outside, 1.00 against 0.20 bits, and names fewer genes, 76% against 95% {C}.

